{"seq":1277,"lane":"A","class":"unsupported-new-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1277.json: “What gross margin will TSMC report for FY2026?”; “The South Korean memory giant is reportedly looking to outsource some base-die production to Intel Foundry beginning with HBM4E”.","rule":"Signed standard §§3–4: a question needs source support for its subject, measure and period, as well as independent investment significance.","mechanism":"A inferred a current-year company-wide margin question from a possible future supplier change; the article gives neither a TSMC margin figure nor a stated effect on FY2026 margin."}
{"seq":1277,"lane":"A","class":"same-fact-two-records","severity":"serious","evidence":"1277.json and _ledger.json: “The South Korean memory giant is reportedly looking to outsource some base-die production to Intel Foundry beginning with HBM4E” is stored as e4438 under v89 and e4440 under v79.","rule":"Signed standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one evidence record, which can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A and B independently returned the same matter, and build_handover appended both without reconciling their overlapping passages."}
{"seq":1277,"lane":"A","class":"same-fact-two-records","severity":"serious","evidence":"1277.json and _ledger.json: “TSMC’s HBM4 base die is estimated to cost three to four times more than an SK Hynix-produced core DRAM die” is stored as e4439 under v89 and e4441 under v79.","rule":"Signed standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one evidence record, which can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A and B independently returned the cost comparison; their records survived separately and received different source tiers."}
{"seq":1277,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-original-speaker","severity":"serious","evidence":"1277.json: the passage says “according to a report by Korean outlet Herald Economy”, while B records “original_who”: “SK hynix”.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4: preserve the original speaker and do not invent attribution.","mechanism":"B assigned the subject of the report as the original speaker, although the article does not say SK hynix made that statement."}
{"seq":1278,"lane":"B","class":"future-plan-as-fact","severity":"serious","evidence":"1278.json: “MediaTek will adopt the NVIDIA NVLink Fusion™ platform” is stored with “tier”: “fact”. The same announcement at 1279 is stored as “party_statement”.","rule":"Signed standard §§5.4–5.5: preserve whether a company describes a future plan, and distinguish a party statement from something that has happened.","mechanism":"B classified the announcement of future adoption as an accomplished fact even though its own event_time says “future adoption and product development”."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"A","class":"missing-direct-financial-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"1280.json: “Years Ended June 30, 2026 … Net sales … 39,063,072”, in a table stated to be in thousands; A opened “What net sales will Super Micro Computer (SMCI) report for FY2027” without citing that FY2026 sales figure.","rule":"D371 and signed standard §5.1: retain relevant current financial figures as evidence for the related question.","mechanism":"A selected sales growth and demand passages but omitted the reported sales amount; record preparation nevertheless used $39,063,072,000 as the comparison for the written outcomes."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"A","class":"missing-obligation-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1280.json: “we have current obligations related to non-cancelable purchase commitments of $34.2 billion.” The article also reports FY2026 net sales of $39,063,072 thousand.","rule":"Signed standard §§3 C and 4, D210 and D248 boundary 6: an already-assumed purchase commitment large enough to change cash or credit risk can open an amount question for the next annual report.","mechanism":"A proposed sales and margin questions but no question about the disclosed commitments. The commitment passage occurs within the text sent to A; the trace does not establish why A omitted it."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"incorrect-ladder-arithmetic","severity":"serious","evidence":"1280.json v90: “FY2027 net sales are within 5% above or below FY2026 reported net sales of $39,063,072,000”, with lo 37009918400 and hi 41015825600.","rule":"Signed standard §3 requires checkable, non-overlapping outcomes; META_SYSTEM requires numerical bounds to express the stated conditions.","mechanism":"The 95% and 105% values are $37,109,918,400 and $41,016,225,600. check_bounds verifies adjacent numeric bounds, but does not check the calculation against the written comparison."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"rung-boundary-mismatch","severity":"serious","evidence":"1280.json v90: “FY2027 net sales are more than 20% above FY2026 reported net sales of $39,063,072,000” has inclusive lo 46875686400; the adjacent outcome says “up to 20% above” but has exclusive hi 46875686400.","rule":"Signed standard §3 requires mutually exclusive, checkable outcomes; META_SYSTEM defines lower bounds as inclusive and upper bounds as exclusive.","mechanism":"The numeric partition and the written conditions disagree at exactly $46,875,686,400; check_bounds checks the numeric partition without comparing it with the conditions."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"A","class":"same-fact-two-records","severity":"serious","evidence":"1280.json and _ledger.json: “During fiscal year 2026, the computer server industry experienced supply constraints for certain components” is stored as e4447 under v90 and e4453 under v91.","rule":"Signed standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one evidence record, which can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A supplied the same passage separately for both candidates; build_handover created a separate evidence record for each passage."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"B","class":"increase-misstated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1280.json quotes “increased billing for Hyper Servers, GPU & Super Racks of $15,261.5 million or 83.4% compared to prior year”; B summarizes this as “driven primarily by $15.3 billion of Hyper Servers, GPU and Super Racks”.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4: preserve what a figure measures in a standalone record.","mechanism":"B’s summary drops that $15.3 billion is the year-over-year increase, making it read as the total sales amount."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"A","class":"article-truncated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1280.json: “Purchase Commitments - We have agreements to purchase inventory and non-inventory items primarily through the next 12 months. As of June 30, 2026, these remaining non-cancelable commitments were $ 34.2 billion”; this passage begins after character 400,000.","rule":"D199 and docs/DECISIONS.md §6: each item is read whole by its extraction request.","mechanism":"split_seven_day_poc.py item_requests and metadata_request slice the article at extraction.MAX_TEXT_CHARS, which is 400,000. The earlier portion separately reports the $34.2 billion commitment, but the later passage’s inventory and timing details were not sent."}
